DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'parserRadioButtons.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

$rb1 = RadioButtons(
    [
        [ 'marital status', 'mean TV viewing time', 'TV viewing time' ],
        'None of the above'
    ],
    2,
    labels => 'ABC'
);

$rb2 = RadioButtons(
    [
        [
            'married people and single people',
            'married men and married women',
            'men and women'
        ],
        'None of the above'
    ],
    1,
    labels => 'ABC'
);

$rb3 = RadioButtons(
    [ [ 'men and women', 'married couples' ], 'None of the above' ],
    1, labels => 'ABC');

$rb4 = RadioButtons(
    [
        [
            'the difference between the TV viewing times of a married couple',
            'the difference between the TV viewing times of men and women'
        ],
        'None of the above'
    ],
    0,
    labels => 'ABC'
);

BEGIN_PGML
Suppose you want to use a paired sample to compare the mean TV viewing times of married men and married women. 

a) What is the variable under consideration? [_]{$rb1}
b) What are the two populations under consideration? [_]{$rb2}
c) What are the pairs? [_]{$rb3}
d) What is the paired-difference variable? [_]{$rb4}


END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
a) Because you want to study the TV viewing time, then this is the variable. *[$rb1]****
b) The two populations are married men and married women. *[$rb2]****
c) The pairs are married couples.  *[$rb3]****
d) The paired-difference variable is the difference between the TV viewing times of a married couple. *[$rb4]****
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();        # This should be the last executable line in the problem.